## Decision Record

- Extend `project_projection.py`; do not create a second project-world builder.
- Generate and track `work/100k.md` as a deterministic read-only orientation surface comparable to
  the existing indexes. Authoritative edits continue through current Tool Shed artifacts and state.
- Use existing artifact identity and outcome/closure semantics as the accountability ledger. Do not
  invent 100k item IDs or dispositions.
- Compute recommendations from existing planning order and campaign/cycle state; never invent an
  owner priority or silently perform the recommended cycle.
- Treat existing overview, queue, planning-order, and loop commands as drill-down machine APIs.
- Keep DisplayTest migration and hosted write-back out of this milestone.

## Recovery Contract

- Rendering is atomic and deterministic. A failed refresh leaves the prior `work/100k.md` intact.
- Check mode compares exact expected bytes and fails on stale or manually edited projection content.
- Unknown authority, malformed focus-area or project state, projection truncation that would hide
  required accounting, or invalid relationships fails closed with a controlled diagnostic.
- The renderer performs no lifecycle, planning, relationship, outcome, release, or hosted mutation.
- Work2 deployment uses only the configured development targets and preserves their project work.

## Verification Strategy

- Focused tests for concise sections, exhaustive identity coverage, attention and change signals,
  deterministic bytes, atomic refresh, stale detection, and read-only behavior.
- File- and SQLite-authority fixtures proving the same contract and explicit feature limits.
- Existing project-projection, dashboard, planning, campaign, loop, work-state, and manifest checks.
- Repository validator, strict Doctor, and checkpoint/rebuild parity.
- Exact-candidate web-development deployment plus released-snapshot update and changed-behavior
  checks in the approved Linux and Windows test beds, followed by release-cohort registration.

## Authority Boundaries

This roadmap authorizes faithful planning, source/test/documentation changes, local commits, known
development deployment, focused qualification, release-cohort registration, and checkpointing at
Work2 under the current project preference. It does not authorize production promotion, release,
publication, credentials, destructive recovery, unknown targets, DisplayTest mutation, hosted
write-back, or retirement of the drill-down machine APIs.
